{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/905279-sidereals-wfhl-peerless-masters-of-the-martial-arts-crystal-chameleon-style","id":905279,"title":"[Sidereals:WFHL] Peerless Masters of the Martial Arts: Crystal Chameleon Style","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-01T17:27:04-07:00","id":905279,"title":"[Sidereals:WFHL] Peerless Masters of the Martial Arts: Crystal Chameleon Style","content":"This ancient Celestial martial art dates back to the Primordial War, when it was innovated and used by the Chosen of Mercury to help deliver vital messages despite overwhelming Primordial opposition. Demons and Lintha alike were left blinking and confused as practitioners quickly blurred through their blockades, leaving only footprints and corpses to mark their passing. It is still strongly favored today for its mixture of surprise and speed. Those who have fought a Blinding Prism (as practitioners of this style are known) rarely know precisely what hit them, and that suits the needs of the Viziers of the Second Age perfectly. Unbeknown to its Sidereal inventors, the style is also widely popular in Autochthonia.<br /> <br /> <b>Crystal Chameleon Weapons:</b> The Blinding Prism favors flexibility and reach; in addition to unarmed attacks, she may use the spear, rope dart, weighted rope or their artifact equivelents.<br /> <br /> <b>Armor:</b> Crystal Chameleon Style is incompatible with armor.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/5wv9eTX.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Just Another Branch Deceit</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts : Crystal Chameleon Style 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> Radiating Essence through his chakras in a precisely controlled array, the martial artist breaks light around herself, creating intermittent highlights of illumination and shadow throughout the area which help draw attention away from herself. Just Another Branch Deception enhances her ability to re-establish surprise during combat (Exalted p. 203), converting all dice added from a stunt into successes.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Light-Treading Technique</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m, 1wp; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts : Crystal Chameleon Style 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Mastery<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> Extending her anima in an ablative envelope around her, the martial artist eases her passage through the world. On any turn in which she takes her reflexive movement action to move a range band, she gains a bonus of (higher of Essence or 2) dice to any Rush or Disengage roll, and increases her dodge against attacks made from beyond Close range by 1. She may also take her reflexive move while concealed without revealing her position or needing to make repeated stealth rolls, although she still may not rush or disengage without breaking concealment.<br /> <b>Mastery</b>: The martial artist may activate Light-Treading Technique reflexively when they enter Crystal Chameleon Form.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Flashing Passage</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts : Crystal Chameleon Style 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Terrestrial<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Just Another Branch Deceit, Light-Treading Technique<br /> <br /> Collapsing her Essence into pure forward momentum, the martial artist briefly blurs and disappears from sight. While she has Light-Treading Technique active, once per scene, she may enhance a rush or disengage action; if the action is successful, she immediately moves one range band towards or away from her target. This enhanced rush or disengage may be taken while concealed without breaking concealment.<br /> Flashing Passage may be reset by successfully entering stealth while in close range to an opponent.<br /> <b>Terrestrial</b>: Flashing Passage may not be reset.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Crystal Chameleon Form</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 8m; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts : Crystal Chameleon Style 3, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Form<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Flashing Passage<br /> <br /> The martial artist strikes her anima banner, fracturing it into a shifting prism. It becomes impossible to precisely fix her location, imposing a penalty on all attacks and attempts to oppose her stealth actions equal to her anima level; additionally, she suffers no penalties for attempting to reestablish surprise during combat due to her anima, even if her anima would normally make stealth difficult or impossible.<br /> <b>Special activation rules</b>: When the martial artist attacks an enemy from stealth in the same turn as their anima rises to burning or greater, they may reflexively enter Crystal Chameleon Form.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Flashing Leaves Evasion</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 6m; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts : Crystal Chameleon Style 4, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Terrestrial<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Crystal Chameleon Form<br /> <br /> Putting on a sudden burst of speed, the martial artist melts into a blur as an attack closes in on her, briefly disappearing and reappearing to evade the blow. Once per scene, before the dice are rolled for an attack, she may set down up to (Essence + Martial Arts) dice from the attack as 1s. Attackers with effects that allow them to re-roll dice after the attack is made may use these effects freely on the dice that have been set down. Flashing Leaves Evasion may not be used against an attack which is undodgable, striking from ambush, or which consists of uncountable damage.<br /> <b>Terrestrial</b>: Instead of setting the dice down as 1s, you instead may force your opponent to re-roll up to (Essence + Martial Arts) dice on the attack.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Shattered Crystal Rebuke</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m, 3i; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts : Crystal Chameleon Style 5, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Withering-only, Counterattack, Mastery, Perilous<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Flashing Leaves Evasion<br /> <br /> Subjected to attack, the crystal shatters, wounding its attacker rather than defending itself. Shattered Crystal Rebuke may be invoked in response to an attack, whether it strikes the martial artist or not. She vanishes in a blur of speed, reappearing behind her attacker. She may either reflexively attempt to reestablish surprise, even if she would not normally be able to do so, or she may make a withering counterattack. In either case, the reflexive action does not count as the martial artist's action for the turn, and may not be used in response to another counterattack.<br /> <b>Mastery</b>: The martial artist may both attempt to re-establish surprise and launch a withering counterattack, in whichever order she prefers.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Razor-Edged Prism Assault</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 7m; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts : Crystal Chameleon Style 4, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-only, Perilous<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Crystal Chameleon Form<br /> <br /> Accelerating into a flickering blur of unleashed violence, the Blinding Prism strikes a foe from many angles, moving so fast that her attacks seem to occur simultaneously. The martial artist makes up to (higher of Essence or 3) decisive attacks against a single target; her initiative does not reset to base until these attacks are concluded. After a successful attack, the martial artist subtracts her successes from her remaining initiative; after a failed attack, she loses 2 initiative. After each attack, successful or failed, she loses an additional 2 initiative. If the martial artist incapacitates her target, the effect ends and any remaining attacks are lost. If the martial artist enters initiative crash, the effect ends, any remaining attacks are lost, and she does not reset to base initiative.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Death from Nowhere Method</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m, 1wp; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts : Crystal Chameleon Style 5, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Dual<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Razor-Edged Prism Assault<br /> <br /> In one moment the battlefield is serene; in the next, the martial artist has already struck. Death from Nowhere Method may only be used to enhance an attack made from surprise. If it enhances a withering attack, the martial artist doubles her post-soak damage. If it enhances a decisive attack, the martial artist may ignore hardness and adds (lower of Essence or extra successes on her attack) to the raw damage of the blow<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Stepping Beyond Light Prana</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts : Crystal Chameleon Style 5, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Mastery<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Shattered Crystal Rebuke, Death from Nowhere Method<br /> <br /> The martial artist focuses her Essence into her lungs then breathes it out into her anima, which shivers into a kaleidoscope that expands to intermittently flicker through an area within Close range of her, roughly centered on the martial artist and moving with her. While this emphatically announces the Blinding Prism's general presence, it also conceals her precise location. She may always attempt to establish surprise, even if the attempt would normally be impossible due to a lack of cover or concealment options. Any non-area attack which depends on sight when targeting her has a 50% chance of failing, striking one of the flickering colors instead of her. Roll a single d10 before making the attack; the attack automatically misses if the roll is 1 - 5.<br /> The effects of Stepping Beyond Light Prana are suspended when the martial artist attacks until her next action. The charm ends if the martial artist is dealt damage by a decisive attack.<br /> <b>Mastery</b>: The martial artist may activate Stepping Beyond Light Prana reflexively in response to being attacked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":169,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","user":"wastevens","date":". 06-02-2016, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T17:41:05-07:00","id":905284,"title":"","content":"I was trying to do this myself for a while with my Alchemicals homebrew, before I just gave up and used Ironheart Destroyer. Great job!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T18:12:51-07:00","id":905297,"title":"","content":"The form looks overpowered. Its cheaper than Snake Form and there is no inherent trade-off for racking your anima up to bonfire level for a scene-length -3 penalty to attacks.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T18:21:47-07:00","id":905303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/905279-sidereals-wfhl-peerless-masters-of-the-martial-arts-crystal-chameleon-style?p=905297#post905297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The form looks overpowered. Its cheaper than Snake Form and there is no inherent trade-off for racking your anima up to bonfire level for a scene-length -3 penalty to attacks.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hm. Fair point; I'll bump it to 8m.<br /> <br /> There are a few trade offs relative to Snake form tho- considerably less soak (no armor vs light armor + dexterity), and an interesting limit on many of the more powerful charms, which consume anima levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T18:22:44-07:00","id":905304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/905279-sidereals-wfhl-peerless-masters-of-the-martial-arts-crystal-chameleon-style?p=905284#post905284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was trying to do this myself for a while with my Alchemicals homebrew, before I just gave up and used Ironheart Destroyer. Great job!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sincere question; what problems did you run into while trying the conversion? I'm curious about points of convergent / divergent thinking <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T18:35:40-07:00","id":905309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/905279-sidereals-wfhl-peerless-masters-of-the-martial-arts-crystal-chameleon-style?p=905304#post905304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sincere question; what problems did you run into while trying the conversion? I'm curious about points of convergent / divergent thinking <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just really getting the same feel and general idea of the style from 2.Xe itself. The multi-action charm and dodge charms proved to be challenges for me as I had ideas, I looked at Ebon Shadow, and saw they were nearly the same and went &quot;...Shit.&quot; I never had many ideas after that. The only thing I got really settled on was getting the form effects down, which was a -2 penalty to attacks/awareness rolls to spot you and ability to reestablish surprise in your anima/bright light sources, but it left a sour taste in my mouth as it was always nitpicking me that it could be more.<br /> <br /> The phrase &quot;You're your own worst critic&quot; rings true with me very much so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T00:08:44-07:00","id":905437,"title":"","content":"Is the anti-synergy of Just Another Branch Deceit with the Sid excellency intentional?<br /> Also, 3m for what amounts to +1 sux on one specific kind of roll is fairly narrow for something you'll spend 8 xp on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some of me humble homebrew for ex3:<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hOOjEGyoq3owLoUwIwTfWKTffzo_udsiUTwomw7wudA/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Artifacts for Crumple's DB homebrew</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tI2T1Re0G8QOuoXkH7Y4PrKQxk1BPEGpbi82SpkTyIw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Some Lintha QCs</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1O2I_2iWTCflJ36ggkDvjTeXmzFsGHKRxAi6L_Ry6g4w/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A Wyld Behemoth</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8838-tds","name":"TDS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T03:53:29-07:00","id":905527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TDS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/905279-sidereals-wfhl-peerless-masters-of-the-martial-arts-crystal-chameleon-style?p=905437#post905437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the anti-synergy of Just Another Branch Deceit with the Sid excellency intentional?<br /> Also, 3m for what amounts to +1 sux on one specific kind of roll is fairly narrow for something you'll spend 8 xp on.</div> </div> </div> </div>The original effect did not really play well in E3 (providing three or four bonus successes for 4m on attempts to establish surprise); they'd either have to be specified as cap-breaking (which would be O.O) or be little better than a hyper-efficient Stealth excellency for Solars and almost completely worthless for Sidereals- both of which seemed like suboptimal solutions. So a new solution was needed. <br /> <br /> I like charms that increase the rewards from stunting, especially actions that aren't always the easiest to stunt in the first place, as they can go a long ways to enhancing the feel of a style or branch. I waffled back and forth on 'double stunt dice' or 'convert stunt dice to successes', and opted on the later, since stealth benefits more from greater consistency than a higher ceiling- while sometimes, you need to get 20 successes, more often you just need to *not* fail to get three or four.<br /> <br /> Also, it's more like adding 2 dice than 1 die, since even a one point stunt adds two dice (which would be converted to 2 successes)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T04:47:07-07:00","id":905547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/905279-sidereals-wfhl-peerless-masters-of-the-martial-arts-crystal-chameleon-style?p=905527#post905527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The original effect did not really play well in E3 (providing three or four bonus successes for 4m on attempts to establish surprise); they'd either have to be specified as cap-breaking (which would be O.O) or be little better than a hyper-efficient Stealth excellency for Solars and almost completely worthless for Sidereals- both of which seemed like suboptimal solutions. So a new solution was needed. <br /> <br /> I like charms that increase the rewards from stunting, especially actions that aren't always the easiest to stunt in the first place, as they can go a long ways to enhancing the feel of a style or branch. I waffled back and forth on 'double stunt dice' or 'convert stunt dice to successes', and opted on the later, since stealth benefits more from greater consistency than a higher ceiling- while sometimes, you need to get 20 successes, more often you just need to *not* fail to get three or four.<br /> <br /> Also, it's more like adding 2 dice than 1 die, since even a one point stunt adds two dice (which would be converted to 2 successes)</div> </div> </div> </div>I like increasing the rewards for stunting, but all this does is reward people for getting at least a one point stunts, which you'll get in 99%. This charm looks more like it encourages minimal effort stunts, since even the most minimal of stunts grants the botch-protection good stunts usually grant.<br /> Why not scale the benefit with stunt level?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some of me humble homebrew for ex3:<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hOOjEGyoq3owLoUwIwTfWKTffzo_udsiUTwomw7wudA/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Artifacts for Crumple's DB homebrew</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tI2T1Re0G8QOuoXkH7Y4PrKQxk1BPEGpbi82SpkTyIw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Some Lintha QCs</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1O2I_2iWTCflJ36ggkDvjTeXmzFsGHKRxAi6L_Ry6g4w/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A Wyld Behemoth</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8838-tds","name":"TDS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T05:48:19-07:00","id":905562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/905279-sidereals-wfhl-peerless-masters-of-the-martial-arts-crystal-chameleon-style?p=905303#post905303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. Fair point; I'll bump it to 8m.<br /> <br /> There are a few trade offs relative to Snake form tho- considerably less soak (no armor vs light armor + dexterity), and an interesting limit on many of the more powerful charms, which consume anima levels.</div> </div> </div> </div> The latter part is not so apparent as none of the charms use a in their costs or state that they reset the anima to dim level.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T05:54:17-07:00","id":905564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TDS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/905279-sidereals-wfhl-peerless-masters-of-the-martial-arts-crystal-chameleon-style?p=905547#post905547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like increasing the rewards for stunting, but all this does is reward people for getting at least a one point stunts, which you'll get in 99%. This charm looks more like it encourages minimal effort stunts, since even the most minimal of stunts grants the botch-protection good stunts usually grant.<br /> Why not scale the benefit with stunt level?</div> </div> </div> </div>Two things;<br /> First, the gap between stunt rewards is narrower than it used to be.<br /> Second, I feel that the value proposition (botch protection, reduced variance, slight cap breaking vs narrow focus, slightly more expensive than excellency, lack of synergy with Sidereal TN manipulation) is about right for an entry level charm in a martial art.<br /> <br /> I mean, we can disagree on this- but I don't think a reward for stunting is going to discourage people from trying for 2 or 3 point stunts.<br /> <br /> (Plus, stunting to establish surprise is already more difficult, since you have to describe the experience of something that is not intended to be experienced. It's not like, super hard or anything, but 2 and 3 point stunts are going to be less common IME)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T05:56:06-07:00","id":905565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/905279-sidereals-wfhl-peerless-masters-of-the-martial-arts-crystal-chameleon-style?p=905562#post905562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The latter part is not so apparent as none of the charms use a in their costs or state that they reset the anima to dim level.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a limit on charms within Crystal Chameleon Style itself, but with charms from outside the style that want to use the anima as a resource.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T22:57:25-07:00","id":906227,"title":"","content":"Then I am dubious about that being used as a balancing factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T04:05:20-07:00","id":906312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/